/* ⚠ THE PAIRINGS ARE REAL — the only thing on this page that is. Pulled live
   2026-08-10: 48 rows across 46 songs, every essay published, two songs
   (Digital Society, Second Nature) carrying two essays each. Unlike the
   feelings, nothing here is invented, because nothing here needed to be —
   Michael has been pairing music to writing since Squarespace and the corpus
   already holds it.

   THIS IS THE PAIRING READ BACKWARDS. On an essay, the song appears under the
   title: *press play, then read* (ADR-0009's third role). The relation has
   always been legible in exactly one direction, and the data is symmetric. So
   the room can say the other half — *this song carries that piece* — for free,
   with no new column, no new tagging, and no new concept. It is also the one
   thing here a playlist structurally cannot hold: a playlist has no second
   column, and no essay to put in it. */
